## Telegram Node Features Demonstrated

### Parse Modes
- **HTML**: Rich formatting with tags (&lt;b&gt;, &lt;i&gt;, &lt;code&gt;)
- **Markdown**: Lightweight markup syntax
- **MarkdownV2**: Advanced markdown features (extensible)

### Configuration Options
- **Environment Variables**: TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
- **Node Configuration**: chat_id, bot_token override
- **Retry Logic**: 1-5 configurable attempts
- **Notification Control**: Silent message option

### Message Types
- **Notifications**: Status updates and alerts
- **Progress Reports**: Dynamic workflow updates
- **Error Alerts**: System failure notifications  
- **Completion Reports**: Success confirmations

### Advanced Features
- **Variable Substitution**: Dynamic content insertion
- **Character Escaping**: Safe HTML/Markdown rendering
- **Conditional Logic**: Message routing based on conditions
- **Error Handling**: Retry mechanisms and failure management
- **Template Support**: Reusable message formats

### Use Cases
- **Workflow Notifications**: Start/completion alerts
- **Error Monitoring**: System failure notifications
- **Progress Tracking**: Real-time status updates
- **User Communication**: Personalized messages
- **System Integration**: API response forwarding
- **Automation Alerts**: Scheduled task notifications

### Integration Patterns
- **Fire-and-Forget**: Asynchronous message delivery
- **Variable Integration**: Dynamic content from workflow
- **Conditional Messaging**: Logic-based notifications
- **Error Recovery**: Graceful failure handling
- **Multi-Format Support**: HTML and Markdown options

This example demonstrates the complete Telegram messaging capabilities of flowsh, enabling robust communication and notification features in automated workflows.

